To solve this, we first find the value of $g(-3)$. We substitute $x = -3$ into $g(x)$:
\begin{align*}
g(-3) &= 3(-3) + 4 \\
&= -9 + 4 \\
&= -5
\end{align*}
Now we have $g(-3) = -5$. Next, we need to find the value of $f(g(-3))$, which is the same as $f(-5)$. We substitute $x = -5$ into $f(x)$:
\begin{align*}
f(-5) &= (-5)^2 \\
&= 25
\end{align*}
Therefore, $f(g(-3)) = \boxed{25}$.</think> <answer>25</answer>

